<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · North America and Oceania</p><h1 class="st-title">Palau</h1><p class="st-meta">1994 CE – present · capital Ngerulmud</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A western Pacific island republic of about 340 islands, in free association with the United States, the last part of the Trust Territory to reach independence.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Palau was part of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/trust-territory-of-the-pacific-islands">Trust Territory of the Pacific Islands</a>. Its voters rejected the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/federated-states-of-micronesia">Federated States of Micronesia</a>, and it approved a constitution and became the Republic of Palau on 1 January 1981. The Compact of Free Association, signed in 1982, entered into force on 1 October 1994, ending the trusteeship.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Palau is a presidential republic under its 1981 constitution, with the president as head of state and government and a bicameral Palau National Congress. It has no military of its own and relies on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> for defence under the Compact. The economy is based on tourism, subsistence agriculture and fishing, and foreign aid, with the US dollar as currency. In 2009 Palau created the world's first shark sanctuary, announced by President Johnson Toribiong.</p><h2>To the present</h2><p>Surangel Whipps Jr is the president. In 2012 the Rock Islands were declared a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a>, and in 2017 Palau introduced the Palau Pledge, stamped on passports. In February 2021 it withdrew from the Pacific Islands Forum after a dispute over the election of its secretary-general.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/palau.jpg" alt="Palau" width="330" height="207"><figcaption>Image: Original: John Blau Skebong Vector: Nightstallion · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Palau.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1994 CE – present</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/21st-century"